1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,943
Two new touches just landed in Shelfie.

2
00:00:02,943 --> 00:00:09,790
Books can have real cover pictures, and a review assistant helps the grown up give kind, useful feedback.

3
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:11,891
Nia adds The Hobbit.

4
00:00:11,891 --> 00:00:16,521
She types the title, picks a colour and a sticker, then chooses a picture.

5
00:00:16,521 --> 00:00:19,150
The preview shows her cover straight away.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,609
The book goes on her shelf with its picture, right next to the others.

7
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:28,728
A grown up can change a cover any time from Manage book.

8
00:00:28,728 --> 00:00:31,430
The new picture appears as soon as it uploads.

9
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:36,364
Over in Review, Dad opens a chapter and presses Help me review.

10
00:00:36,364 --> 00:00:41,939
The assistant flags short answers that deserve a conversation, with a reason for each.

11
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:45,052
It also drafts an encouraging note.

12
00:00:45,052 --> 00:00:50,200
Dad can use it as it is, or make it his own, pick a sticker, and send it to Nia.

13
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,890
Nothing is sent until Dad says so, and if the assistant is ever unavailable, reviewing works just as before.

